/*Q9. Write a Java program to calculate an employee's tax deduction and net salary using a static nested class, constructor, and instance methods.
The provided EmployeeTax class must contain a static nested class named Employee.
Employee class
Declare the following private instance variables:
• empld (String): stores the employee ID.
• name (String): stores the employee name.
• salary (double): stores the employee's salary.
Constructor
Implement a parameterized constructor Employee(String emplId, String name, double salary) to initialize all three instance variables using
the this keyword.
Methods
Implement the following methods in the Employeeclass:
• display(): Prints the employee ID, name, and salary on separate lines. The salary must be formatted to exactly two decimal places.
• calculateTax(): Calculates the tax using the formula:
tax = salary * 10 / 100
• Print the tax rounded to exactly two decimal places.
• calculateNetSalary(): Calculates the net salary using the formula:
netSalary = salary - tax
• Print the net salary rounded to exactly two decimal places.
The EmployeeTax class should read the employee ID, name, and salary, create an Employee object, and call display(), calculateTax(), and
calculateNetSalary() in that order.
Input Format:
• The first line contains a string representing the employee id.
• The second line contains a string representing the employee name.
• The third line contains a floating-point number representing the salary.
Output Format:
• Print the output of display(), followed by calculateTax(), followed by calculateNetSalary() on separate lines, each rounded to two
decimal places.
*/
import java.util.Scanner;
 
public class EmployeeTax {
 
    static class Employee {
        private String empId;
        private String name;
        private double salary;
 
        Employee(String empId, String name, double salary) {
            this.empId = empId;
            this.name = name;
            this.salary = salary;
        }
 
        void display() {
            System.out.println(empId);
            System.out.println(name);
            System.out.printf("%.2f%n", salary);
        }
 
        double calculateTax() {
            double tax = salary * 10 / 100;
            System.out.printf("%.2f%n", tax);
            return tax;
        }
 
        void calculateNetSalary() {
            double tax = salary * 10 / 100;
            double netSalary = salary - tax;
            System.out.printf("%.2f%n", netSalary);
        }
    }
 
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
        String id = sc.nextLine().trim();
        String name = sc.nextLine().trim();
        double salary = Double.parseDouble(sc.nextLine().trim());
        Employee e = new Employee(id, name, salary);
        e.display();
        e.calculateTax();
        e.calculateNetSalary();
        sc.close();
    }
}
